This code fix the linear sampling. But in writing it I realized that we are not basically duplicating taps in a way that we don't want to do. Since PCF5 and PCF13 work in 1 pixel offsets we end up reading each tap twice (except for the first and the last). PC5 would take 10 taps when only 6 are needed and PCF13 would take 26 taps when only 14 are needed. 

